CANDIDATE_TC = 'HIROMETRICS, INC.\nCANDIDATE TERMS OF SERVICE AND USER AGREEMENT\nVersion 1.1 | Last Updated: July 2026 | Pilot Edition\n\nIMPORTANT — PLEASE READ CAREFULLY BEFORE CREATING AN ACCOUNT OR USING THIS PLATFORM\n\nTHIS AGREEMENT CONTAINS IMPORTANT PROVISIONS INCLUDING A BINDING ARBITRATION CLAUSE, A CLASS ACTION WAIVER, LIMITATIONS ON LIABILITY, AND CONSENT TO DATA COLLECTION AND VERIFICATION ACTIVITIES. BY CREATING AN ACCOUNT, YOU ACKNOWLEDGE THAT YOU HAVE READ, UNDERSTOOD, AND AGREE TO BE LEGALLY BOUND BY ALL TERMS AND CONDITIONS SET FORTH HEREIN.\n\nIF YOU DO NOT AGREE TO THESE TERMS IN THEIR ENTIRETY, YOU MAY NOT CREATE AN ACCOUNT OR USE THE HIROMETRICS PLATFORM.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 1. DEFINITIONS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nFor purposes of this Agreement, the following terms shall have the meanings set forth below:\n\n1.1 "Company," "HiroMetrics," "we," "us," or "our" refers to HiroMetrics, Inc., a Delaware corporation, and its affiliates, subsidiaries, successors, and assigns.\n\n1.2 "Platform" means the HiroMetrics web application, mobile applications, APIs, and any associated services, tools, or portals made available by the Company, including all updates, upgrades, and enhancements thereto.\n\n1.3 "User," "Candidate," "you," or "your" means any individual who registers for, accesses, or uses the Platform in a candidate capacity.\n\n1.4 "Account" means the registered account created by a Candidate upon acceptance of these Terms.\n\n1.5 "Profile" means the collection of personal, professional, educational, and credentialing information submitted by a Candidate through the Platform.\n\n1.6 "Baseline Profile" means the immutable, locked version of a Candidate\'s Profile as it existed at the time of initial submission and locking through the Platform.\n\n1.7 "Submission" means any act by which a Candidate forwards or makes available their Profile or Resume to a Hiring Entity through the Platform.\n\n1.8 "Resume" means any curriculum vitae, resume document, or equivalent document uploaded by a Candidate to the Platform.\n\n1.9 "User Content" means any information, data, text, images, photographs, documents, files, certifications, credentials, or other materials submitted, uploaded, posted, or transmitted by a Candidate through the Platform, including but not limited to Profile photographs, government-issued identification documents, academic transcripts, professional certifications, and Resume files.\n\n1.10 "Hiring Entity" means any employer, staffing firm, consulting agency, managed service provider, vendor management system operator, or other organization that receives or reviews a Candidate\'s Profile or Submission through the Platform.\n\n1.11 "Intermediary" means any staffing agency, subcontractor, recruitment process outsourcer, or other third-party organization that participates in the transmission of a Candidate\'s Submission within a multi-tier hiring chain.\n\n1.12 "Verification Services" means the identity verification, credential authentication, document validation, biometric comparison, employment history verification, education verification, professional license verification, and related services conducted by the Company or its Third-Party Verification Partners.\n\n1.13 "Third-Party Verification Partners" means any identity verification providers, background screening firms, biometric technology vendors, credentialing authorities, or other service providers engaged by the Company to perform Verification Services.\n\n1.14 "Consistency Report" means any report generated by the Platform that compares information submitted in a Candidate\'s current Submission against the Candidate\'s Baseline Profile for the purpose of identifying discrepancies, inconsistencies, or material changes.\n\n1.15 "Effective Date" means the date on which a Candidate accepts these Terms by clicking "Accept and Continue" or otherwise affirmatively consenting to this Agreement.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 2. ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS AND ELIGIBILITY\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n2.1 Acceptance. By clicking "Accept and Continue," creating an Account, or otherwise accessing or using the Platform, you represent that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by this Agreement and any additional policies, guidelines, or rules incorporated herein by reference, including the HiroMetrics Privacy Policy. This Agreement constitutes a binding legal contract between you and HiroMetrics.\n\n2.2 Eligibility. You represent and warrant that: (a) you are at least eighteen (18) years of age; (b) you have the legal capacity and authority to enter into this Agreement; (c) you are not prohibited by applicable law from using the Platform; and (d) your use of the Platform will comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws, rules, and regulations.\n\n2.3 Account Registration. To access certain features of the Platform, you must create an Account. You agree to provide accurate, current, and complete information during registration and to update such information as necessary to maintain its accuracy. You are solely responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your Account credentials and for all activities that occur under your Account.\n\n2.4 One Account Per Individual. Each individual may maintain only one (1) active Account. Creating duplicate or multiple accounts is prohibited and may result in immediate termination of all associated accounts.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 3. USER CONTENT — ACCURACY, OWNERSHIP, AND LICENSE\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n3.1 Accuracy Obligation. You represent, warrant, and covenant that all User Content you submit through the Platform — including but not limited to your name, contact information, employment history, educational background, certifications, professional licenses, references, and any uploaded documents — is accurate, truthful, current, and complete to the best of your knowledge. You acknowledge that the integrity of the Platform depends upon the veracity of information submitted by Candidates.\n\n3.2 Prohibition on Misrepresentation. You expressly agree that you will not submit, upload, or otherwise provide through the Platform any information or document that is false, misleading, fabricated, altered, forged, or misrepresentative in any material respect. Without limiting the foregoing, you shall not: (a) claim academic credentials, degrees, or certifications you did not earn; (b) misrepresent dates, titles, responsibilities, or scope of employment; (c) submit documents that have been altered or counterfeited; (d) use another person\'s identity or credentials; (e) submit User Content that infringes the intellectual property rights of any third party; or (f) represent that you possess skills, qualifications, or immigration status that you do not in fact hold.\n\n3.3 Your Ownership. Subject to the license granted herein, you retain ownership of User Content that you submit to the Platform. HiroMetrics does not claim ownership of your personal information or Profile data.\n\n3.4 License Grant to HiroMetrics. By submitting User Content to the Platform, you hereby grant HiroMetrics a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free, sublicensable license to access, store, process, reproduce, display, transmit, analyze, and share your User Content solely for the purposes of: (a) operating and providing the Platform and its features; (b) conducting or facilitating Verification Services; (c) generating Consistency Reports; (d) transmitting your Profile and Submissions to Hiring Entities and Intermediaries to whom you have directed a Submission; and (e) complying with applicable legal obligations. This license survives termination of your Account to the extent necessary to fulfill the foregoing purposes.\n\n3.5 Responsibility for User Content. You acknowledge and agree that you are solely responsible for all User Content that you submit through the Platform. HiroMetrics does not endorse, verify (except through its Verification Services), or take responsibility for the accuracy of User Content prior to verification.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 4. BASELINE PROFILE AND IMMUTABILITY\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n4.1 Baseline Locking. Upon your voluntary submission and locking of your Profile, the information recorded at that time constitutes your Baseline Profile. The Baseline Profile serves as the permanent, attributable record against which all future Submissions will be compared.\n\n4.2 Immutability of Baseline. Once locked, your Baseline Profile cannot be altered, deleted, or revised except through a formal correction request process established by HiroMetrics. You acknowledge that the immutability of the Baseline Profile is a core feature of the Platform designed to ensure the integrity and reliability of the credentialing record.\n\n4.3 Consistency Monitoring. HiroMetrics may generate Consistency Reports comparing information in any Submission you make against your Baseline Profile. Any material discrepancies identified through this comparison may be flagged, documented, and disclosed to Hiring Entities and Intermediaries who have received your Submission, as described in Article 5.\n\n4.4 Correction Requests. If you believe that information contained in your Baseline Profile is inaccurate due to a genuine error, you may submit a correction request to HiroMetrics. All correction requests are subject to review, verification, and approval by HiroMetrics at its sole discretion. Approved corrections will be annotated in the record rather than overwriting the original Baseline.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 5. DATA USE FOR VERIFICATION — CONSENT\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n5.1 Consent to Verification. By creating an Account and uploading any User Content to the Platform — including but not limited to Profile photographs, government-issued identification documents, academic transcripts, professional certifications, diplomas, licenses, immigration documents, and Resume files — you expressly and irrevocably grant HiroMetrics and its authorized Third-Party Verification Partners the right and license to use such User Content, on an ongoing basis, for the purpose of:\n\n   (a) verifying your identity, including through facial recognition, biometric comparison, liveness detection, and photographic matching technologies;\n   (b) authenticating the genuineness, validity, and accuracy of documents you have submitted, including through optical character recognition, metadata analysis, and direct inquiry with issuing authorities;\n   (c) verifying the accuracy and completeness of your employment history, including contacting former employers or their authorized agents directly;\n   (d) verifying the accuracy and completeness of your educational history, including contacting educational institutions or their authorized agents directly;\n   (e) verifying the validity, currency, and authenticity of any professional licenses, certifications, or credentials you have claimed, including contacting the issuing bodies or registries directly;\n   (f) verifying your legal authorization to work, immigration status, or other regulatory requirements relevant to placement in a position; and\n   (g) any other verification activities reasonably related to the evaluation of your professional qualifications and identity.\n\n5.2 Independent and Requested Verification. You acknowledge and agree that Verification Services may be initiated: (a) by HiroMetrics at any time, at its own discretion, as part of its platform integrity operations; or (b) at the request of a Hiring Entity or Intermediary to whom you have submitted your Profile through the Platform. You consent to both forms of initiation without requiring additional notice for each individual verification event.\n\n5.3 Consent to Third-Party Disclosures. You authorize HiroMetrics and its Third-Party Verification Partners to contact, communicate with, and obtain information from any of the following parties in connection with Verification Services: (a) your former and current employers; (b) educational institutions from which you claim to have received degrees, certifications, or other credentials; (c) professional licensing bodies, certification boards, and trade organizations; (d) government agencies or registries; and (e) any other issuing authority of credentials referenced in your Profile.\n\n5.4 Further Consents. You agree, upon request by HiroMetrics or any Third-Party Verification Partner, to provide any additional written consents, release forms, or authorizations that may be required under applicable law or by a third-party source in order to facilitate Verification Services. Your failure or refusal to provide such additional consents may limit the scope of Verification Services and may be disclosed to relevant Hiring Entities as a limitation on the verification record.\n\n5.5 Profile Photographs. Profile photographs uploaded by Candidates are stored solely for the purpose of visual identity reference by Hiring Entities during the evaluation and interview process. This allows Hiring Entities to visually confirm that the individual they are interviewing or meeting corresponds to the person represented in the submitted profile. HiroMetrics does not perform automated facial recognition, biometric analysis, or any algorithmic processing of photographs. Photographs are used as a manual, advisory reference tool only. You consent to your profile photograph being displayed to Hiring Entities and Intermediaries to whom you have directed a Submission.\n\n5.6 Document Media. You acknowledge that non-photograph documents you upload to the Platform — including resumes, certificates, transcripts, and other files — may be processed using automated technologies including but not limited to optical character recognition (OCR) for the purposes of credential verification and consistency checking as described in this Article 5.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 6. SHARING WITH HIRING ENTITIES AND MULTI-TIER CHAINS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n6.1 Consent to Share. By directing a Submission to any Hiring Entity or Intermediary through the Platform, you explicitly consent to your Profile, Resume, User Content, Consistency Report, and verification results being shared with: (a) the Hiring Entity to which the Submission was directed; (b) any Intermediaries in the transmission chain between the originating submitting party and the Hiring Entity; and (c) any affiliates or authorized personnel of such Hiring Entities and Intermediaries who have a legitimate need-to-know in connection with the evaluation of your candidacy.\n\n6.2 Chain-of-Custody Transparency. You acknowledge that the Platform maintains a chain-of-custody record of all Submissions and transmission events, including the identities of parties who have received or forwarded your Profile within the hiring chain. This transparency is a designed feature of the Platform intended to protect both candidates and hiring parties.\n\n6.3 Retention by Hiring Entities. HiroMetrics is not responsible for the retention, use, or processing of your information by Hiring Entities or Intermediaries after it has been transmitted to them. Each Hiring Entity and Intermediary is independently responsible for its own data practices and compliance with applicable privacy and employment laws.\n\n6.4 Withdrawal of Submission. You may request withdrawal of an active Submission prior to a final hiring decision. However, you acknowledge that HiroMetrics cannot guarantee the deletion or return of information already accessed or downloaded by a Hiring Entity or Intermediary prior to receipt of a withdrawal request.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 7. PROHIBITED CONDUCT\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n7.1 You agree that you will not use the Platform to:\n\n   (a) Submit any false, fraudulent, fabricated, plagiarized, or misrepresentative information or documentation;\n   (b) Impersonate any other person or entity, or misrepresent your identity in any way;\n   (c) Circumvent, disable, or interfere with security features of the Platform, including any features that prevent or restrict use or copying of any content;\n   (d) Engage in any automated data collection, scraping, crawling, or extraction from the Platform without the express written consent of HiroMetrics;\n   (e) Upload or transmit any virus, malware, Trojan horse, or other malicious code through the Platform;\n   (f) Use the Platform for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable federal, state, or local law or regulation;\n   (g) Engage in any conduct that restricts or inhibits any other person from using or enjoying the Platform;\n   (h) Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any portion of the Platform, other accounts, computer systems, or networks connected to HiroMetrics;\n   (i) Create multiple accounts or assist others in doing so; or\n   (j) Use the Platform in any manner that could damage, disable, overburden, or impair the Platform\'s infrastructure.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 8. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n8.1 HiroMetrics Property. The Platform, including its design, architecture, software, algorithms, trademarks, service marks, trade names, logos, and all content created by HiroMetrics (collectively, "HiroMetrics IP"), is and shall remain the exclusive property of HiroMetrics. Nothing in this Agreement grants you any right, title, or interest in or to any HiroMetrics IP.\n\n8.2 Restrictions. You shall not copy, reproduce, distribute, modify, create derivative works of, publicly display, publicly perform, republish, download, store, or transmit any HiroMetrics IP without the prior written consent of HiroMetrics.\n\n8.3 Feedback. Any feedback, suggestions, or ideas you provide to HiroMetrics regarding the Platform shall become the exclusive property of HiroMetrics. You hereby assign all right, title, and interest in such feedback to HiroMetrics.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 9. PRIVACY AND DATA PROTECTION\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n9.1 Privacy Policy. Your use of the Platform is also governed by HiroMetrics\' Privacy Policy, which is incorporated herein by reference. The Privacy Policy describes how HiroMetrics collects, uses, stores, and protects your personal information, including your rights with respect to such data under applicable law.\n\n9.2 Data Retention. HiroMetrics will retain your Profile data and Baseline Profile for a period reasonably necessary to fulfill the purposes set forth in these Terms, to comply with legal obligations, to resolve disputes, and to enforce its agreements. Upon Account termination or deletion, HiroMetrics will follow its data retention and deletion procedures as described in the Privacy Policy, subject to any legal hold obligations.\n\n9.3 Illinois Privacy Laws. To the extent HiroMetrics collects biometric information, it does so in compliance with the Illinois Biometric Information Privacy Act (BIPA) and any other applicable state biometric privacy statutes. HiroMetrics will provide any required separate written disclosures and obtain any required additional consents prior to the collection of biometric data to the extent required by applicable law.\n\n9.4 California Privacy Rights. To the extent applicable, California residents may have additional rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), including the right to know, the right to delete, the right to opt-out of sale, and the right to non-discrimination. Please refer to the Privacy Policy for further details.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 10. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTIES\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n10.1 AS-IS BASIS. THE PLATFORM AND ALL SERVICES PROVIDED HEREUNDER ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE," WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS, IMPLIED, STATUTORY, OR OTHERWISE. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, HIROMETRICS EXPRESSLY DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO: (a) IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT; (b) WARRANTIES THAT THE PLATFORM WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, ERROR-FREE, OR FREE OF VIRUSES OR OTHER HARMFUL COMPONENTS; (c) WARRANTIES AS TO THE ACCURACY, COMPLETENESS, OR RELIABILITY OF ANY CONTENT OR DATA ON THE PLATFORM; AND (d) WARRANTIES THAT THE RESULTS OF VERIFICATION SERVICES WILL BE ACCURATE, COMPLETE, OR FREE FROM ERROR.\n\n10.2 No Employment Guarantee. HiroMetrics makes no representation or warranty that use of the Platform will result in any employment offer, contract, or placement. Hiring decisions are made solely by Hiring Entities and are outside the control of HiroMetrics.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 11. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n11.1 EXCLUSION OF CERTAIN DAMAGES. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL HIROMETRICS, ITS OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, AGENTS, LICENSORS, OR SERVICE PROVIDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY: (a) INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, PUNITIVE, OR EXEMPLARY DAMAGES; (b) LOSS OF PROFITS, REVENUE, DATA, GOODWILL, OR BUSINESS OPPORTUNITIES; (c) DAMAGES ARISING FROM HIRING DECISIONS MADE BY THIRD PARTIES BASED ON YOUR PROFILE OR VERIFICATION RESULTS; OR (d) DAMAGES ARISING FROM UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS TO OR ALTERATION OF YOUR USER CONTENT OR ACCOUNT.\n\n11.2 AGGREGATE CAP. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, HIROMETRICS\' TOTAL CUMULATIVE LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ANY CLAIMS ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THIS AGREEMENT OR THE PLATFORM SHALL NOT EXCEED THE GREATER OF: (a) THE TOTAL AMOUNT PAID BY YOU TO HIROMETRICS IN THE TWELVE (12) MONTHS PRECEDING THE CLAIM; OR (b) ONE HUNDRED U.S. DOLLARS ($100.00).\n\n11.3 Essential Basis. You acknowledge that the limitations of liability in this Article 11 reflect a reasonable allocation of risk and are an essential basis of the bargain between you and HiroMetrics. HiroMetrics would not provide the Platform without these limitations.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 12. INDEMNIFICATION\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n12.1 You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless HiroMetrics and its officers, directors, employees, agents, licensors, and service providers from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, judgments, awards, losses, costs, expenses, or fees (including reasonable attorneys\' fees) arising out of or relating to: (a) your violation of this Agreement; (b) your submission of false, fraudulent, or misrepresentative User Content; (c) your violation of any applicable law, rule, or regulation; (d) your infringement of the intellectual property or other rights of any third party; or (e) any dispute between you and any Hiring Entity or Intermediary.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 13. ACCOUNT SUSPENSION AND TERMINATION\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n13.1 Termination by HiroMetrics. HiroMetrics reserves the right, in its sole discretion, to suspend or permanently terminate your Account at any time, with or without notice, for any reason, including but not limited to: (a) a violation of any provision of this Agreement; (b) submission of materially false, fraudulent, or misrepresentative information; (c) conduct that HiroMetrics determines, in its sole judgment, is harmful to the Platform, other users, Hiring Entities, or the reputation of HiroMetrics; or (d) a request by law enforcement or regulatory authorities.\n\n13.2 Consequences of Termination. Upon termination: (a) your right to access and use the Platform will immediately cease; (b) HiroMetrics may retain your data as described in the Privacy Policy and as required by law; and (c) any provisions of this Agreement that by their nature should survive termination shall survive, including without limitation Articles 3, 4, 5, 8, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15, and 16.\n\n13.3 Fraud Reporting. In cases where HiroMetrics determines that a Candidate has submitted materially fraudulent information, HiroMetrics reserves the right to notify relevant Hiring Entities and Intermediaries who have received or reviewed the Candidate\'s Profile, subject to applicable law.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 14. DISPUTE RESOLUTION — BINDING ARBITRATION\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n14.1 Agreement to Arbitrate. EXCEPT AS OTHERWISE PROVIDED IN THIS ARTICLE, YOU AND HIROMETRICS AGREE THAT ANY DISPUTE, CLAIM, OR CONTROVERSY ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THIS AGREEMENT OR THE PLATFORM (COLLECTIVELY, "DISPUTES") SHALL BE RESOLVED EXCLUSIVELY THROUGH FINAL AND BINDING ARBITRATION, RATHER THAN IN COURT.\n\n14.2 Class Action Waiver. YOU AND HIROMETRICS AGREE THAT EACH MAY BRING CLAIMS AGAINST THE OTHER ONLY IN AN INDIVIDUAL CAPACITY AND NOT AS A PLAINTIFF OR CLASS MEMBER IN ANY PURPORTED CLASS, REPRESENTATIVE, OR COLLECTIVE ACTION PROCEEDING.\n\n14.3 Arbitration Procedure. Arbitration shall be conducted by JAMS or the American Arbitration Association (AAA) under its applicable rules, as selected by HiroMetrics. The arbitration shall take place in Chicago, Illinois, or, at your election, may be conducted remotely. The arbitrator\'s decision shall be final and binding and may be entered as a judgment in any court of competent jurisdiction.\n\n14.4 Opt-Out. You may opt out of the arbitration agreement by sending written notice to legal@hirometrics.com within thirty (30) days of first accepting these Terms. Opting out does not affect any other provision of this Agreement.\n\n14.5 Exceptions. Nothing in this Article shall prevent either party from seeking injunctive or other equitable relief in a court of competent jurisdiction to prevent irreparable harm.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 15. GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n15.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Illinois, without regard to its conflict of law provisions. To the extent any dispute is not subject to arbitration under Article 14, the parties consent to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts located in Cook County, Illinois.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 16. MODIFICATIONS TO THESE TERMS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n16.1 HiroMetrics reserves the right, in its sole discretion, to modify, update, supplement, or replace these Terms and Conditions at any time. When material changes are made, HiroMetrics will notify you by: (a) displaying a prominent notice within the Platform; (b) sending an email notification to the address associated with your Account; or (c) requiring acknowledgment upon your next login to the Platform.\n\n16.2 Affirmative Acceptance. Continued use of the Platform following notification of a material change to these Terms may require your affirmative acceptance of the updated Terms as a condition of continued access. If a new version of the Terms is presented to you upon login and you decline to accept, your access to the Platform will be suspended until acceptance is provided or your Account is closed.\n\n16.3 Non-Acceptance. If you do not agree to any revised or updated version of these Terms, you must immediately discontinue all use of the Platform and may request deletion of your Account in accordance with the Privacy Policy.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 17. GENERAL PROVISIONS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n17.1 Entire Agreement. This Agreement, together with the Privacy Policy and any other policies or agreements incorporated herein by reference, constitutes the entire agreement between you and HiroMetrics with respect to the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior or contemporaneous agreements, representations, or understandings.\n\n17.2 Severability. If any provision of this Agreement is found to be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable under applicable law, such provision shall be modified to the minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable, and the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.\n\n17.3 Waiver. No failure or delay by HiroMetrics in exercising any right or remedy under this Agreement shall constitute a waiver of such right or remedy.\n\n17.4 Assignment. You may not assign or transfer any of your rights or obligations under this Agreement without the prior written consent of HiroMetrics. HiroMetrics may freely assign this Agreement in connection with a merger, acquisition, reorganization, or sale of all or substantially all of its assets.\n\n17.5 Notices. All notices to HiroMetrics under this Agreement should be directed to: legal@hirometrics.com or by mail to HiroMetrics, Inc., Chicago, Illinois.\n\n17.6 No Third-Party Beneficiaries. This Agreement is for the sole benefit of you and HiroMetrics and does not create any third-party beneficiary rights.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nACKNOWLEDGMENT\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nBY CLICKING "ACCEPT AND CONTINUE," YOU ACKNOWLEDGE THAT YOU HAVE READ THIS AGREEMENT IN ITS ENTIRETY, THAT YOU UNDERSTAND ITS TERMS, AND THAT YOU AGREE TO BE LEGALLY BOUND BY ALL OF ITS PROVISIONS, INCLUDING THE ARBITRATION AGREEMENT AND CLASS ACTION WAIVER IN ARTICLE 14.\n\n© 2026 HiroMetrics, Inc. All rights reserved.'

EMPLOYER_TC = 'HIROMETRICS, INC.\nEMPLOYER AND HIRING ENTITY TERMS OF SERVICE\nVersion 1.0 | Last Updated: June 2026\n\nIMPORTANT — PLEASE READ CAREFULLY BEFORE CREATING AN ACCOUNT OR USING THIS PLATFORM\n\nBY CREATING AN ACCOUNT OR ACCESSING CANDIDATE PROFILES THROUGH THE HIROMETRICS PLATFORM, YOU REPRESENT THAT YOU HAVE THE AUTHORITY TO BIND YOUR ORGANIZATION TO THESE TERMS AND THAT YOUR ORGANIZATION AGREES TO BE LEGALLY BOUND BY THIS AGREEMENT.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 1. DEFINITIONS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n1.1 "Company," "HiroMetrics," "we," "us," or "our" refers to HiroMetrics, Inc.\n\n1.2 "Platform" means the HiroMetrics web application, APIs, and all associated services.\n\n1.3 "Hiring Entity," "Employer," "you," or "your" means any organization or individual accessing the Platform in an employer, staffing firm, agency, or Hiring Entity capacity.\n\n1.4 "Candidate Data" means any profile information, User Content, verification results, Consistency Reports, or other data relating to a candidate accessed through the Platform.\n\n1.5 "Authorized User" means any employee, contractor, or agent of the Hiring Entity authorized to access the Platform on its behalf.\n\n1.6 "Consistency Report" means the report generated by HiroMetrics comparing a candidate\'s current Submission against their Baseline Profile.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 2. ACCOUNT AND ACCESS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n2.1 You represent and warrant that you have the authority to bind your organization to this Agreement. You are responsible for ensuring that all Authorized Users comply with this Agreement and all applicable laws.\n\n2.2 You agree to maintain the confidentiality of your Account credentials and to promptly notify HiroMetrics of any unauthorized access to your Account.\n\n2.3 You agree to use the Platform only for lawful hiring, screening, and candidate evaluation purposes in connection with genuine employment or contracting opportunities.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 3. PERMITTED USE OF CANDIDATE DATA\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n3.1 Permitted Purposes. You agree to access and use Candidate Data solely for the purpose of evaluating candidates for legitimate employment, contracting, or staffing opportunities and for no other purpose.\n\n3.2 Prohibited Uses. You expressly agree that you will not: (a) use Candidate Data for any purpose other than candidate evaluation; (b) sell, license, transfer, or disclose Candidate Data to any unauthorized third party; (c) use Candidate Data in a manner that violates any applicable employment, privacy, anti-discrimination, or data protection law; (d) attempt to contact candidates through means or for purposes outside the scope of the hiring process without the candidate\'s consent; or (e) use Candidate Data to build or enrich any proprietary database or talent pool without the express written consent of HiroMetrics and the relevant candidates.\n\n3.3 Non-Discrimination. You agree to use Candidate Data in compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local equal employment opportunity and anti-discrimination laws, including the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, and any applicable state equivalents.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 4. VERIFICATION SERVICES AND CONSISTENCY REPORTS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n4.1 Informational Only. Verification results and Consistency Reports provided through the Platform are for informational purposes only and do not constitute a guarantee, warranty, or representation by HiroMetrics as to a candidate\'s suitability, qualifications, fitness for any position, or legal authorization to work.\n\n4.2 Independent Decisions. All hiring, contracting, and placement decisions are made solely by you and remain your exclusive responsibility. HiroMetrics is not a party to any employment relationship and is not responsible for any hiring decision made based on information obtained through the Platform.\n\n4.3 Requesting Verification. By requesting verification services for a candidate through the Platform, you represent that you have a permissible purpose under applicable law and that any required candidate consents have been obtained or are being obtained through the Platform\'s consent mechanisms.\n\n4.4 Not a Consumer Reporting Agency. HiroMetrics is not a consumer reporting agency as defined under the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA), and the Platform does not provide consumer reports as defined thereunder. You agree not to use information from the Platform as a substitute for FCRA-compliant background screening where such screening is legally required.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 5. CONFIDENTIALITY AND DATA SECURITY\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n5.1 Confidentiality. You agree to treat all Candidate Data accessed through the Platform as confidential and proprietary. You will implement and maintain commercially reasonable administrative, technical, and physical security measures to protect Candidate Data against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction.\n\n5.2 Data Breach Notification. In the event of any actual or reasonably suspected unauthorized access to or disclosure of Candidate Data, you agree to: (a) promptly notify HiroMetrics in writing; (b) cooperate with HiroMetrics in investigating and mitigating the breach; and (c) comply with all applicable data breach notification laws.\n\n5.3 Retention and Deletion. You will retain Candidate Data only for as long as necessary for the purposes for which it was collected and as required by applicable law. Upon request by HiroMetrics or a candidate, you will delete or destroy Candidate Data in a commercially reasonable manner, except to the extent retention is required by law.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 6. COMPLIANCE WITH APPLICABLE LAW\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n6.1 You are solely responsible for ensuring that your use of the Platform and any hiring decisions comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws and regulations, including but not limited to: (a) the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA); (b) Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; (c) the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA); (d) the Age Discrimination in Employment Act (ADEA); (e) the Immigration Reform and Control Act (IRCA); (f) applicable state and local ban-the-box, fair chance, and salary history laws; and (g) applicable data privacy and protection laws, including the Illinois Personal Information Protection Act and any applicable state data privacy statutes.\n\n6.2 You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless HiroMetrics from any claims, penalties, fines, or liabilities arising from your failure to comply with applicable law in connection with your use of the Platform or any hiring decision.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 7. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n7.1 The Platform and all HiroMetrics IP are and remain the exclusive property of HiroMetrics. You are granted a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to access and use the Platform solely for the purposes described in this Agreement. You shall not copy, reverse engineer, decompile, or create derivative works from any part of the Platform.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 8. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTIES\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n8.1 THE PLATFORM AND ALL SERVICES ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. HIROMETRICS DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. HIROMETRICS DOES NOT WARRANT THAT VERIFICATION RESULTS OR CONSISTENCY REPORTS ARE COMPLETE, ACCURATE, OR FREE FROM ERROR.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 9. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n9.1 IN NO EVENT SHALL HIROMETRICS BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, PUNITIVE, OR SPECIAL DAMAGES, INCLUDING LOST PROFITS OR DATA, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE PLATFORM OR ANY HIRING DECISION MADE BASED THEREON. HIROMETRICS\' TOTAL LIABILITY SHALL NOT EXCEED THE GREATER OF THE TOTAL AMOUNTS PAID BY YOU TO HIROMETRICS IN THE PRECEDING TWELVE (12) MONTHS OR ONE HUNDRED DOLLARS ($100.00).\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 10. MODIFICATIONS TO THESE TERMS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n10.1 HiroMetrics reserves the right to modify these Terms at any time. Material changes will be communicated by notice within the Platform or by email. Continued use of the Platform following such notification constitutes your acceptance of the updated Terms. If you do not agree to any revised Terms, you must discontinue use of the Platform.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE 11. GENERAL PROVISIONS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n11.1 Governing Law. This Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Illinois without regard to conflict of law provisions.\n\n11.2 Entire Agreement. This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties with respect to the Platform and supersedes all prior agreements or understandings.\n\n11.3 Severability. If any provision is found unenforceable, it shall be modified to the minimum extent necessary, with remaining provisions continuing in full force.\n\n11.4 Assignment. You may not assign this Agreement without HiroMetrics\' prior written consent. HiroMetrics may assign this Agreement in connection with a corporate transaction.\n\n11.5 Contact. For questions: legal@hirometrics.com.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nACKNOWLEDGMENT\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nBY CLICKING "ACCEPT AND CONTINUE," YOU REPRESENT THAT YOU HAVE AUTHORITY TO BIND YOUR ORGANIZATION AND THAT YOUR ORGANIZATION AGREES TO BE LEGALLY BOUND BY THIS AGREEMENT IN ITS ENTIRETY.\n\n© 2026 HiroMetrics, Inc. All rights reserved.'


def upgrade() -> None:
    tc_id = str(uuid.uuid4())

    # Mark any existing current terms as superseded
    op.execute(text(
        "UPDATE terms_versions SET is_current = false WHERE is_current = true"
    ))

    # Insert v1.1 — use get_bind() + dict params for reliable large-text handling
    conn = op.get_bind()
    conn.execute(
        text("""
            INSERT INTO terms_versions
                (id, version_number, content_candidate, content_employer,
                 effective_date, is_current, created_at)
            VALUES (:id, 2, :cand, :emp, NOW(), true, NOW())
        """),
        {"id": tc_id, "cand": CANDIDATE_TC, "emp": EMPLOYER_TC}
    )


def downgrade() -> None:
    op.execute(text("DELETE FROM terms_versions WHERE version_number = 2"))
    op.execute(text(
        "UPDATE terms_versions SET is_current = true WHERE version_number = 1"
    ))
